# KWarner preview PDF (program report printout)

When the user asks for **PDF creation, PDF updates, printout layout, or program-report print changes**, work in the **KWarner locked preview pipeline** — not the web UI unless they explicitly ask for web.

## Pipeline (source of truth)

| Piece | Path |
|-------|------|
| Renderer | `server/pdf/renderProgramReportKwarnerLockedPreview.js` |
| Shared draw helpers | `server/pdf/drawSeminar.js`, `server/pdf/drawFrame.js` |
| Macro signal data | `js/foodPlanPrintout.js` |
| Payload | `js/programReportPrintout.js` + `js/kwarnerLockedPreviewFixtures.js` |

## Mandatory after every PDF change

1. Run **`npm run render:kwarner-preview`**
2. Script writes **two new files** (never overwrites):
   - **Primary:** `docs/samples/kwarner-locked-preview-kristi-N.pdf` (N increments: …-9, …-10, …)
   - **Archive:** `docs/samples/kwarner-preview-kristi-veg-fruit-vN.pdf`
3. Copy primary file to `/opt/cursor/artifacts/` when that folder exists (secondary).
4. **Commit and push to `main`** so the raw download URL works immediately.

## What to give the user

**One link only — the raw download URL.** It saves straight to Mac Downloads. Do **not** use `github.com/.../blob/...` (that opens GitHub in the browser).

After push to `main`, paste:

`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/koryedwards-del/landing-burn-and-build/main/docs/samples/<locked-filename>`

Also refresh `docs/samples/kwarner-locked-preview-kristi-latest.pdf` each render so this stable link always serves the newest file:

`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/koryedwards-del/landing-burn-and-build/main/docs/samples/kwarner-locked-preview-kristi-latest.pdf`

State the exact versioned filename too (e.g. `kwarner-locked-preview-kristi-24.pdf`). Do not use the artifacts panel.
